\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The viability geometry, in cross-section perpendicular to the stasis axis $s$ (looking down the axis; $\bar  {\bm  {s}}$ at the centre). Each threshold $\{\cos (\bm  {x},s)\ge \theta \}$ is a disc: the \emph  {viable region} $\Omega $ ($\cos \ge 0.70$), its \emph  {convex contractive core} $\Omega _A$ ($\cos \ge 0.88$), and the \emph  {stasis cone} ($\cos \ge 0.95$, half-angle $18.2^\circ $) around the deterministic fixed point $\bar  {\bm  {s}}$. $\Omega $ is non-convex: the concave entropy bound indents its boundary (top right), which is why the existence argument (Theorem~\ref {thm:hybrid_invariance}) is carried on the convex core $\Omega _A$, where $f_0$ contracts on average ($\lambda _{\max }<0$; arrows). A sustained perturbation drives an excursion out of $\Omega _A$ that is confined and returns (orange), never leaving $\Omega $. The measured spectrum (Sec.~\ref {sec:ly01}) and EXP-NS-01 (Sec.~\ref {sec:sustained_noise}) discharge the contraction and confinement claims respectively.}}{11}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:omega_nested}{{1}{11}{The viability geometry, in cross-section perpendicular to the stasis axis $s$ (looking down the axis; $\bar {\bm {s}}$ at the centre). Each threshold $\{\cos (\sv ,s)\ge \theta \}$ is a disc: the \emph {viable region} $\Omega $ ($\cos \ge 0.70$), its \emph {convex contractive core} $\Omega _A$ ($\cos \ge 0.88$), and the \emph {stasis cone} ($\cos \ge 0.95$, half-angle $18.2^\circ $) around the deterministic fixed point $\bar {\bm {s}}$. $\Omega $ is non-convex: the concave entropy bound indents its boundary (top right), which is why the existence argument (Theorem~\ref {thm:hybrid_invariance}) is carried on the convex core $\Omega _A$, where $f_0$ contracts on average ($\lambda _{\max }<0$; arrows). A sustained perturbation drives an excursion out of $\Omega _A$ that is confined and returns (orange), never leaving $\Omega $. The measured spectrum (Sec.~\ref {sec:ly01}) and EXP-NS-01 (Sec.~\ref {sec:sustained_noise}) discharge the contraction and confinement claims respectively}{figure.caption.7}{}}
\newlabel{thm:hybrid_invariance}{{1}{11}{Hybrid invariance}{theorem.1}{}}
