\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \texttt  {spec\_boot} series under the \textbf  {canonical trust law} (Law~A; \S  \ref {sec:trustlaw}). Convergence holds across scales ($\overline  {dL}\to 0$, every row \texttt  {viable}); $D_\text  {eff}$ stabilises at $6.00$ from 300 ticks onward and \texttt  {stasis\_cos} rises to a plateau $\approx 0.95$ within the contractive core $\Omega _A$ ($\theta _A = 0.88$), rather than to the apex ($\cos = 1$). Cycle counts are identical to the predecessor law, confirming the breath machinery is unchanged. The convergence figures (\ref {fig:lyapunov} and the $D_\text  {eff}$-vs-scale panel) are rendered under this canonical series; the 110-minute long-run observation (\S  \ref {sec:senescence}) predates the trust-law reconciliation and is explicitly badged as predecessor law pending re-measurement (registered re-measurement task, v1.0 round).}}{14}{table.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
