\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces Stationary-measure concentration in $\Omega _A$ vs noise amplitude $\sigma $ (EXP-CORE-01). \emph  {Top:} fraction of $\mu ^*$ inside the contractive core ($\cos \ge \theta _A = 0.88$) --- unity at low noise, leaking only at $\sigma \approx 1.0$ (shaded region). \emph  {Bottom:} minimum cosine observed across all runs plateaus at $0.856 > \theta _\text  {viable}$ from $\sigma \approx 0.3$ onward, confirming $m(\sigma ) > g$ for all tested $\sigma $: the margin axis never becomes the binding constraint under realistic noise.}}{57}{figure.caption.99}\protected@file@percent }
